messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "Global CO2 emissions from energy peak.",
      "detail": "Solar, wind, batteries, and electric vehicles grow fast enough to begin a long decline in fossil fuel use, though emissions decline only slowly at first."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Renewables supply over half of global electricity.",
      "detail": "Solar and wind are the cheapest new power in most regions, and storage deployment accelerates."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "AI systems outperform most humans in routine cognitive work.",
      "detail": "Large-scale automation spreads through administrative, legal, financial, and technical support roles, causing major labor market disruption."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "Sea level rise forces first large managed retreats.",
      "detail": "Several low-lying coastal cities begin relocating districts after repeated tidal flooding and storm surges."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Global average temperature reaches 1.5 degrees Celsius above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Heatwaves and extreme rainfall become noticeably more frequent, and global food production is repeatedly stressed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "A permanent crewed lunar outpost is established.",
      "detail": "International and commercial habitats support rotating crews near the lunar south pole, mainly for science and fuel production."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "First human landing on Mars occurs.",
      "detail": "A joint or commercial mission reaches Mars and returns some crew, proving long-duration deep-space survival."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "Cultivated meat becomes cheaper than factory-farmed meat.",
      "detail": "Lab-grown meat and fermentation-based proteins outcompete conventional livestock in many markets, reducing agricultural emissions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global population peaks near 9.6 billion.",
      "detail": "Falling fertility and aging populations begin to offset longer lifespans and high birth rates in some regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2054,
      "event": "First commercial nuclear fusion plant connects to the grid.",
      "detail": "Fusion provides reliable low-carbon electricity at premium cost initially, later becoming cheaper."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "Carbon dioxide removal reaches gigaton scale.",
      "detail": "Direct air capture, enhanced weathering, and bioenergy with carbon capture remove billions of tons of CO2 per year."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Global average temperature reaches 2.0 degrees Celsius above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Despite mitigation, warming continues; many ecosystems shift and some island states become uninhabitable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "A year-round Mars base is maintained.",
      "detail": "Crews rotate continuously on Mars, and the base begins producing food, water, and oxygen locally."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Global population begins a long, gradual decline.",
      "detail": "Most countries fall below replacement fertility, and migration cannot fully offset local declines."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces become common medical and consumer devices.",
      "detail": "Implants restore lost senses and movement, and healthy users begin using neural interfaces for memory, language, and machine control."
    },
    {
      "year": 2082,
      "event": "First asteroid mining operation returns metals to Earth orbit.",
      "detail": "Platinum-group metals and water from a near-Earth asteroid are processed in space, starting an off-world supply chain."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Sea level has risen about 0.5 meters since 2000.",
      "detail": "Many coastal districts are abandoned or fortified, and ports and cities rebuild further inland."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global biodiversity loss stabilizes after decades of restoration.",
      "detail": "Protected areas, rewilding, and synthetic biology help many ecosystems begin to recover, though extinctions remain high."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Universal basic income or equivalent is standard in most advanced economies.",
      "detail": "Automation and AI produce large economic output, and states guarantee income, services, or resource credits."
    },
    {
      "year": 2160,
      "event": "Human gene editing eliminates most inherited diseases.",
      "detail": "Germline therapies are safe, widely accepted, and regulated; many genetic disorders disappear from the population."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Large-scale ocean alkalinity enhancement begins.",
      "detail": "Efforts to reduce ocean acidification and absorb carbon are deployed across major ocean basins."
    },
    {
      "year": 2260,
      "event": "First interstellar probe is launched toward Proxima Centauri.",
      "detail": "A small robotic probe using fusion or laser sail propulsion begins a decades-long journey to the nearest star system."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Global average temperature stabilizes near 2.5 degrees Celsius above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "A combination of emissions cuts, carbon removal, and limited geoengineering halts further warming."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Mars population reaches one million.",
      "detail": "Sustained immigration and local birth make Mars a self-governing society with growing subsurface cities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "First O'Neill cylinder habitat houses tens of thousands of people.",
      "detail": "Rotating orbital settlements support permanent residents, manufacturing, and agriculture beyond Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Planetary defense system successfully deflects a hazardous asteroid.",
      "detail": "Space-based detection and deflection infrastructure prevents a regional-scale impact."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Heavy industry mostly moves off Earth.",
      "detail": "Mining, refining, and manufacturing occur in orbit, on the Moon, and among asteroids, reducing terrestrial pollution."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Synthetic biology restores most large terrestrial ecosystems.",
      "detail": "Engineered organisms rebuild soils, forests, coral reefs, and wetlands; Earth's biodiversity begins exceeding 21st-century levels."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Average human lifespan exceeds 120 years in wealthy regions.",
      "detail": "Regenerative medicine, gene therapy, and artificial organs extend healthy longevity, though inequality persists."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "First crewed interstellar vessel reaches Proxima Centauri.",
      "detail": "A multi-decade journey begun in the late 2000s or early 3000s delivers a small crew and artificial intelligences to the nearest star system."
    },
    {
      "year": 3400,
      "event": "Human descendants begin diverging into distinct biological and cybernetic populations.",
      "detail": "Different environments, gene editing, and neural augmentation create multiple human-adapted forms, though they remain interfertile."
    },
    {
      "year": 3600,
      "event": "Earth's population stabilizes around 8 billion.",
      "detail": "After a long decline, intentional reproduction policies and new cultural norms produce a stable global population."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Biological and digital cognition become deeply integrated.",
      "detail": "Many individuals are partly non-biological, and identities persist across biological brains, implants, and external systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Mars terraforming begins in earnest.",
      "detail": "Imported nitrogen, greenhouse gases, and engineered biology slowly thicken the Martian atmosphere and warm the planet."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Humanity has self-sustaining settlements across the inner solar system.",
      "detail": "Earth, Moon, Mars, and many orbital habitats are politically diverse but economically integrated."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "A severe but survivable solar storm disrupts global infrastructure.",
      "detail": "A Carrington-scale or larger geomagnetic storm damages power grids and satellites, causing a multi-year crisis, but civilization recovers."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Earth's climate is deliberately managed.",
      "detail": "Planetary engineering maintains a stable, warm climate and high biodiversity."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Human descendants on Mars and orbital habitats are physically distinct.",
      "detail": "Lower gravity and genetic adaptation produce populations that cannot comfortably live on Earth without support."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Human presence extends to the Kuiper belt and Oort cloud.",
      "detail": "Small, mobile habitats and mining probes exploit resources in the outer solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Human descendants live in multiple planetary systems.",
      "detail": "Slow interstellar settlement has established small populations around nearby stars, while Earth remains inhabited as a cultural center."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity likely survives and undergoes dramatic technological, biological, and spatial expansion. By 10000, human-derived intelligences inhabit much of the Solar System and a few nearby star systems, while Earth remains inhabited and culturally central. The path includes climate disruption, automation-driven social strain, and repeated but survivable crises."
}
